<section class="wrap p-sec"><div class="p-two">
  <div class="side"><span class="lbl">School of International and Public Affairs, Columbia University</span><a class="btn" href="https://www.sipa.columbia.edu/communities-connections/faculty/laura-segafredo" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="justify-self:start">Visit faculty profile ↗</a></div>
  <div class="main"><p>My research interests span political economy, ethics, theology, ecology, and the history of economic and political thought. I explore how traditions of moral and political reflection can illuminate contemporary questions of finance, democracy, inequality, climate change, and institutional design, and help us imagine different ways of organizing economic life.</p></div>
</div></section>
